{
  "borough": "Wandsworth",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The air conditioning units, by reason of their size, location and appearance, constitute an unsympathetic and incongruous form of development that result in harm to the character and appearance of the property and the terrace they form part of. The proposal therefore fails to comply with the objectives of the NPPF (2026), policies LP1 and LP5 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and guidance within the Housing SPD (2016).",
    "Reason : 2 - The application has failed to provide sufficient evidence to demonstrate that the operation of the air conditioning units would not result in unacceptable noise and disturbance for neighbouring occupiers.  The proposal therefore fails to comply with policies LP2 and LP14 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023).",
    "Reason : 3 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
